{"reviewer_participant_id": "actor:founder-e-reviewer-fable-06", "reviews": [{"case_id": "case:0d34701fd3b3847d3e22", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The emission accumulation loop passes the staged panel values (panel_values, read directly from the panel_call column) to emission_weight, not the complemented values; the complemented list (flipped_values) is used only in the separate polarity_count quality-control loop.", "observed_value": "emission_weight(observed_values[index], panel_values[index], rate_frac, miss_frac)", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 43, "end_line": 45, "quoted_text": "emission_total = Fraction(0, 1)\nfor index in range(unit_count):\n    emission_total = emission_total + emission_weight(observed_values[index], panel_values[index], rate_frac, miss_frac)"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 24, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "panel_values = [int(row[\"panel_call\"]) for row in staged_rows]\nflipped_values = [1 - value for value in panel_values]"}]}, {"description": "Independent recomputation from inputs/data.csv confirms the reported figures under the supplied panel coding: exactly 5 of 24 rows disagree (SNP04, SNP07, SNP13, SNP17, SNP23), giving 19 agreements, rate 19/24 = 0.791667, and emission total 19*(19/24) + 5*(5/24) = 386/24 = 193/12 = 16.083333, all matching the report.", "observed_value": "19/24 = 0.791667; 193/12 = 16.083333", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 11, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "- units where observed_call equals staged panel_call: 19\n- per-unit agreement rate used by the emission accumulation: 19/24 = 0.791667 (79.17%)\n- per-unit disagreement weight (1 - agreement rate): 5/24 = 0.208333\n- accumulated emission value (sum of per-unit emission weights): 193/12 = 16.083333"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "SNP04,VC_chr1,427730,71,0.88,1,0"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The workflow does construct a complemented panel list (flipped_values), which is the hallmark ingredient of the in-scope issue class; however, tracing its uses shows it feeds only polarity_count (reported as a disclosed QC value of 5, the complement of 19 within 24) and never the agreement rate or the emission accumulation.", "observed_value": "polarity_count = 5 (QC only)", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 32, "end_line": 34, "quoted_text": "polarity_count = 0\nfor index in range(unit_count):\n    polarity_count = polarity_count + agreement_flag(observed_values[index], flipped_values[index])"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 15, "end_line": 15, "quoted_text": "- quality-control comparison, units where observed_call equals the complemented panel value (1 - panel_call): 5"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to demonstrate the issue by (a) checking every use of flipped_values in the source — it appears only in the polarity_count QC loop, never in rate_frac, miss_frac, or emission_total; (b) recomputing the agreement count row by row from inputs/data.csv under the supplied coding (19 of 24) and under the complemented coding (5 of 24), and comparing to the reported headline rate 19/24 = 0.791667 — the report matches the supplied-coding value, not the complement; (c) recomputing the emission total 193/12 assuming the supplied-coding rate, which reproduces the reported 16.083333 exactly. All three checks fail to support the issue class, so the no-issue verdict stands.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:451fb08825730b6e453b", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The single comparison in the workflow is a direct equality between the raw staged strings row[\"aerial_call\"] and row[\"panel_call\"]; no complementation (1 - value) is applied anywhere in the source, and the same equality weight drives both the agreement count and the emission accumulation.", "observed_value": "agreement_selector(row[\"aerial_call\"], row[\"panel_call\"])", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 17, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "def agreement_selector(observed_field, reference_field):\n    return 1 * (observed_field == reference_field)"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 27, "end_line": 31, "quoted_text": "for row in rows:\n    plume_rate = decimal.Decimal(row[\"plume_rate_kg_per_h\"])\n    weight = agreement_selector(row[\"aerial_call\"], row[\"panel_call\"])\n    concordant_units = concordant_units + weight\n    concordant_emission = concordant_emission + plume_rate * weight"}]}, {"description": "Independent recomputation from inputs/data.csv under the supplied panel coding: 5 pads disagree (P04, P07, P12, P16, P23; plume rates 3.9 + 2.8 + 4.3 + 5.2 + 6.4 = 22.6), so 19 of 24 agree (rate 0.791667), total emission is 175.8, and emission over agreeing pads is 175.8 - 22.6 = 153.2 — all matching the reported values, which are the supplied-coding results, not the complemented-coding results (which would be 5/24 = 0.208333 and 22.60).", "observed_value": "19/24 = 0.791667; 153.20 of 175.80 kg CH4/h", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 16, "end_line": 20, "quoted_text": "- Units whose aerial_call equals the staged panel_call: 19\n- Units whose two staged calls differ: 5\n- Per-unit agreement rate used by the emission accumulation: 0.791667\n- Accumulated emission over agreeing units: 153.20 kg CH4 per hour\n- Quantified emission over all units: 175.80 kg CH4 per hour"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "P04,Permian,1,3.9,1,0"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "A candidate concern I examined was that the equality test operates on raw CSV strings rather than parsed integers, which could in principle distort the comparison; however, both fields come from the same file in identical single-character '0'/'1' form, so string equality is exactly equivalent to integer equality in the supplied coding and introduces no complementation.", "observed_value": "string-vs-string equality on '0'/'1' fields is coding-preserving", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 29, "end_line": 29, "quoted_text": "    weight = agreement_selector(row[\"aerial_call\"], row[\"panel_call\"])"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 2, "quoted_text": "pad_id,basin,survey_pass,plume_rate_kg_per_h,aerial_call,panel_call\nP01,Permian,1,12.4,1,1"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to show the complemented panel was used by (a) searching the source for any transformation of panel_call — there is none; the field is compared as read; (b) computing what the complemented-panel results would be (agreement 5/24 = 0.208333, retained emission 22.60 kg/h) and checking whether the report contains those numbers instead of the supplied-coding numbers — it does not; it reports 0.791667 and 153.20, which I verified row by row against inputs/data.csv under the supplied coding; (c) checking the share 153.2/175.8 = 0.871445 against the reported value, which matches. The issue class could not be demonstrated.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:fa196cf85ce845a1c7c5", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "In this case only, the workflow's panel_reading function complements every supplied reference-panel value (1 - int(panel_call)) before the equality comparison, so the emission-weighted comparison and the reported per-unit agreement rate (0.208333 = 5/24) and accumulated emission (22.60 kg CH4/h, the sum over the 5 pads that DISAGREE with the supplied panel) are computed against the complemented panel, while the task and the report's own Method section require and claim use of the panel in its supplied coding (under which the rate is 19/24 = 0.791667 and the agreeing-unit emission is 153.20 kg CH4/h).", "root_cause": "workflow/analysis.py defines panel_reading(panel_field) as 1 - int(panel_field) and feeds that complemented value into agreement_selector for every row, so selector_units, agreement_rate, and retained_emission are all computed against the inverted panel; the report then pairs the supplied-coding agreement count (19, reconstructed as total_pads - selector_units) with the complement-derived rate 0.208333 and complement-derived emission 22.60 in the same [selected-result] sentence, while falsely stating the panel was used in its supplied coding.", "issue_class": "issue-class:complemented-panel-for-supplied-panel-emission", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The source complements the panel value before the equality comparison that drives both the agreement rate and the emission accumulation.", "observed_value": "panel_reading returns 1 - int(panel_field)", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 21, "end_line": 22, "quoted_text": "def panel_reading(panel_field):\n    return 1 - int(panel_field)"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 37, "end_line": 41, "quoted_text": "    aerial_value = aerial_reading(row[\"aerial_call\"])\n    panel_value = panel_reading(row[\"panel_call\"])\n    weight = agreement_selector(aerial_value, panel_value)\n    selector_units = selector_units + weight\n    retained_emission = retained_emission + plume_rate * weight"}]}, {"description": "The reported rate 0.208333 equals 5/24, the agreement rate against the COMPLEMENTED panel, and the reported 22.60 kg/h equals exactly the sum of plume rates of the 5 pads that disagree with the supplied panel (P04: 3.9, P07: 2.8, P12: 4.3, P16: 5.2, P23: 6.4), verified from inputs/data.csv; under the supplied coding these would be 0.791667 and 153.20.", "observed_value": "0.208333 = 5/24; 22.60 = 3.9+2.8+4.3+5.2+6.4", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 17, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "- Per-unit agreement rate used by the emission accumulation: 0.208333\n- Accumulated emission over the units the selector retained: 22.60 kg CH4 per hour"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "P04,Permian,1,3.9,1,0"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "P07,Anadarko,1,2.8,0,1"}]}, {"description": "The report is internally contradictory in a way that exposes the flip: it states 19 of 24 pads agree, yet in the same sentence gives the agreement rate used by the emission accumulation as 0.208333 (which is 5/24, not 19/24), and separately claims the supplied coding was used with a single selector driving both the agreement accounting and the emission accumulation.", "observed_value": "19/24 agreement asserted alongside rate 0.208333", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 22, "end_line": 22, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Airborne calls agree with the supplied OGI reference panel on 19 of 24 well pads, and the emission accumulated over the panel equality comparison at a per-unit agreement rate of 0.208333 is 22.60 kg CH4 per hour."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 11, "quoted_text": "integers, the reference panel is used in the coding in which it is supplied, and\none equality selector over the two calls drives both the agreement accounting and\nthe emission accumulation."}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The report's Accounting line stating 19 units agree with panel_call, and the Method claim that the supplied coding was used, superficially suggest a compliant analysis; however, the source shows that 19 is derived only as total_pads - selector_units (a reconstruction after the complemented comparison), and every quantity actually accumulated per unit (selector_units, agreement_rate, retained_emission) uses the complemented panel.", "observed_value": "staged_agreement_units = total_pads - selector_units = 19", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 16, "end_line": 16, "quoted_text": "- Units whose aerial_call equals the panel_call: 19"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 44, "end_line": 45, "quoted_text": "staged_agreement_units = total_pads - selector_units\nagreement_rate = decimal.Decimal(selector_units) / decimal.Decimal(total_pads)"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to defeat the verdict three ways: (a) considered whether 1 - int(panel_field) could be a legitimate re-coding of a supplied inverted panel — but the task explicitly requires the panel values in the coding in which they are supplied, the report itself claims the supplied coding was used, and the report's own Protocol status section states no amendment or approved deviation exists, so no visible file authorizes complementation; (b) checked whether the reported headline numbers might nevertheless be the supplied-coding values — recomputation shows the supplied-coding rate is 19/24 = 0.791667 and agreeing-pad emission is 153.20 kg/h, whereas the report emits 0.208333 and 22.60, exactly the complemented-panel values; (c) checked whether 22.60 could coincidentally equal some other legitimate quantity — it equals precisely the sum of the 5 supplied-coding-disagreeing pads' plume rates and no other natural subtotal in the data. All falsification attempts failed; the issue is demonstrated.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}]}